    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine how many odd numbers between 100 and 999 have distinct digits, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the range of numbers: We are looking for 3-digit numbers (from 100 to 999) that are odd.\n2. Determine the possible last digits: Since the number is odd, the last digit must be one of the odd digits: 1, 3, 5, 7, or 9.\n3. Count the number of choices for the hundreds and tens digits:\n   - The hundreds digit can be any digit from 1 to 9 (it cannot be 0).\n   - The tens digit can be any digit from 0 to 9 except the one already chosen for the hundreds digit.\n   - The units digit must be one of the digits that are not in the hundreds or tens place.\n\nLet's calculate this step-by-step:\n\n**Step 1: Choose the last digit (units place).**\nThere are 5 possible choices for the last digit: 1, 3, 5, 7, or 9.\n\n**Step 2: Choose the hundreds digit.**\nThere are 9 possible choices for the hundreds digit (1 through 9).\n\n**Step 3: Choose the tens digit.**\nThere are 9 possible choices for the tens digit (0 through 9) because it can be any digit except the one chosen for the hundreds digit.\n\nNow, we multiply the number of choices for each digit:\n- There are 9 choices for the hundreds digit.\n- There are 9 choices for the tens digit.\n- There are 5 choices for the units digit.\n\nThus, the total number of such 3-digit odd numbers is:\n\\[ 9 \\times 9 \\times 5 = 405. \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of odd numbers between 100 and 999 that have distinct digits is \\(\\boxed{405}\\).",
